   "kind": "misconception",
   "stage": ["question"],
   "text": {
    "en": "Why do bad things happen? Start with care, not a lecture. The Qur'an says Allah tests people with fear, loss and hardship, gives good news to the patient, never burdens a soul beyond its capacity, and that with hardship comes ease. We cannot always say why a particular thing happened to a particular person, and it is wrong to tell someone their suffering was a punishment."
   },
   "ageBand": ["adult"],
   "tags": ["misconception", "doubt", "suffering", "qadar"],
   "triggers": ["why do bad things happen", "why does god allow suffering", "why is there evil"],
   "doNotSay": ["If the person is grieving, offer presence first; never say a loss was a punishment."],
